PROVISIONAL (proposed to Guillaume Duboc; replace it with his fix when there is one).
Tallying did not terminate on systems whose solutions are recursive through function
types with variable decorations (the jobs of Section 2 with an undecorated job): node
ids embed substitutions and states whose generators are closures, so hashing or
comparing a node traverses an exponentially larger tree, and emptiness checks, which
remember only the keys on the current path and restart without them in some places
(the fast paths of phi_starter/4, simplify_polymorphic/1), descend forever.
1. Nodes are interned in the process dictionary: a node is {n, :node, :node}, mapped to
   its id, state and generator; the same id gives the same node; unfoldings are cached;
   the ids of lazy nodes and the comparison of systems no longer contain closures.
   Nodes are therefore local to the process that built them.
2. Emptiness results are memoized in the process dictionary at the points where a key
   enters seen (nodes and the BDDs of functions, lists, maps and tuples), as in
   Algorithm 2 of "Implementing Set-Theoretic Types": a key being checked is assumed
   empty; when its check fails, every positive result recorded since is rolled back
   (negative results are kept); when the outermost check succeeds, the results are
   definitive.
3. syntactic_vars/1: the variables that occur in a type, without the equivalence checks
   of vars/1.

